Changed how a visitor's address is read from `X-Forwarded-For`: the audit log and the magic-link rate limit now take its last entry, because the leftmost is whatever the client sent, and that let a client forge the logged address and take a fresh rate-limit bucket on every request. The header is read when `client_ip_headers` is empty and Zope's `trusted-proxy` is not set; with `trusted-proxy` set, the address is the one `request.getClientAddr()` reports. A site reachable without its proxy has to set `trusted-proxy` or name a header its proxy overwrites. Upgrade step 1012 creates the setting, empty. `client_ip` moved from `pas.plugins.identity.core.services.magiclink` to `pas.plugins.identity.core.utils.clientip`. @ericof
